  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Founding and Governance
    
    Grand Auditor Mingmeyang led the first Aurora Stack settlers to establish Promenade Hei during the Frozen Peace, transforming what began as a refugee encampment into a functioning surface colony. She leads the Qingqe'frostlings, the governing council that seized and held Promenade Hei through demonstrated competence and willingness to act where others would not. That she mastered five disciplines of ice-craft and aurora-channeling — **Ice-whisper (shimmer)**, **Slide Prism**, **Snowdrift-numb (astral)**, **Soar Helm**, and **The Mechanism Refine** — speaks less to ambition than to the fact that no one else could be spared to learn them.
    
    Her flippers bear the geometric crystalline scars of Slide Prism calibration. An aurora-glass circlet sits perpetually crooked on her head. The crystal beneath her skin glows pale blue, dimming visibly by evening — the sign of a practitioner who expends more aurora-light than she absorbs. Her robes are white, silver-trimmed, fraying at the cuffs.
    
    ## The Shell Hatch and Deterioration
    
    When the colony faced resource collapse, Mingmeyang judged that dependence on a single practitioner for krill-bloom mapping was untenable. She permitted Beacon-Keeper Lianhinglou to seek knowledge beyond the Flipper Accord's boundaries — a decision whose consequences are detailed in the chronicle *Forty-Seven Days of Margin*. Lianhinglou's venture into the forbidden chambers of Wane Oncea yielded **The Shell Hatch**, a sixth discipline Mingmeyang adopted at significant cost. Lianhinglou lost memories. Both practitioners bear crystalline scarring beyond what their other practices explain. Lianhinglou insists Mingmeyang never asked them to stop.
    
    Accounts from Promenade Hei now reference Mingmeyang's deterioration alongside whispers of corruption — whether ice-corruption from the colony's breach-points or the more figurative kind, the sources do not cleanly distinguish.
    
    ## Character
    
    Zhinghoua lang'Gleam, her first pioneer and the closest thing Mingmeyang has to family, brings fire-tea each evening. Mingmeyang accepts it and forgets to drink it. She still wakes believing Promenade Hei will collapse without her constant attention. She has not tested the hypothesis. She is beloved, and she is slowly hollowing out.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
