  annotation "note_1771590680477_1", anchor: "whether ice-corruption from the colony's breach-points or the more figurative kind, the sources do not cleanly distinguish", text: "They cannot distinguish because the distinction may not exist. Ice-whisper (shimmer) burns aurora-light to create rifts in the berg's memory. Snowdrift-numb enters and potentially alters frozen moments. A practitioner exercising both disciplines regularly is not merely exposed to corruption — she is performing operations indistinguishable from it. The sources fail to separate Mingmeyang's deterioration from Promenade Hei's corruption because Mingmeyang's practice is one of Promenade Hei's breach-points. I wrote the entry knowing this. The main text's ambiguity is not imprecision. It is the most honest thing in it.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
